# Engine demo: every directive of the visual-novel stage in one short script.
# Not a story (the leading underscore keeps it out of the picker and the manifest).
# Preview: ?src=stories/_demo-effects.vn   (add &autoplay=N to land on a stop)

@title The Stage, Tried Out
@kind blog
@source A demo of the Paper Theatre directives
@status draft
@palette night
@note A test card for the engine. Nothing here is quoted from anywhere.
@cast Aoi name="Aoi" hue=345 long cardigan skin=1
@cast Ren name="Ren" hue=215 short glasses coat skin=2
@cast Mika name="Mika" hue=150 ponytail hoodie skin=3
@cast Model name="the Model" lattice=sparse hue=192
@cast You player hue=30

@bg sakura
@fx petals on
@mode nvl
Every spring the hill behind the school does this, and every spring somebody stops to look.
This page is NVL mode: lines gather on a full page over the dimmed picture.
(A line wrapped in parentheses is a thought. It is set in italics, in a softer colour.)
@page
A page break clears it. Then the story goes back to the window at the bottom.
@mode adv

@chapter 1 The Hill
@show Aoi left (smile)
Aoi (smile): You came. I was starting to think the petals would be gone first.
@show Ren right (thinking)
Ren (thinking): The active speaker is lit. The other one dims and waits.
Aoi (laugh): He always explains the stage directions out loud.
@thumb
Ren (deadpan): Somebody has to.
@show Mika center (surprised) far
Mika (surprised): A third sprite, standing further back.
@move Mika right
@move Ren center
Mika (smile): And now we have changed places.
@hide Mika
@show Aoi left near
Aoi (worried): Closer. Is this too close?
@show Aoi left
* It is fine. -> fine
* A little. -> little

== fine
Aoi (smile): Good.
-> after

== little
Aoi (puzzled): Noted.
-> after

== after
@hide all
@fx none
@transition fade 900
@bg classroom dusk
The classroom at dusk, reached through black.
@flashback on Spring, the study room
@fx dust on
@show Aoi center (neutral)
Aoi: This is a memory: sepia, grain, letterbox bars, a caption in the corner.
(I remember the dust more than the lesson.)
@flashback off
@hide all
@fx none

@chapter 2 Transitions
@transition dissolve 700
@bg rooftop
Dissolve, the default.
@transition white 900
@bg sea
White, through light.
@transition wipe-left 800
@bg station
Wipe-left.
@transition wipe-right 800
@bg corridor
Wipe-right.
@transition iris 900
@bg studio
Iris.
@transition blinds 900
@bg room
Blinds.
@transition cut
@bg garden
Cut.

@scene Weather
@bg night
@fx snow on
Snow.
@fx snow off
@fx rain on
Rain.
@fx rain off
@fx fireflies on
Fireflies.
@fx none
@fx shake
A shake.
@fx flash
A flash.
@fx pulse
A pulse.
@pause 600

@chapter 3 Illustrations
@transition fade 800
@cg tree | The tree on the hill
A full-screen illustration replaces the background and the sprites while it is shown.
@cg desk-night
The desk, at night.
@cg screen-code
One identifier someone left readable.
@cg hands-keyboard
Hands on the keys.
@cg two-chairs
Two chairs.
@cg corridor-light
A corridor, and light at the end of it.
@cg page
A page.
@cg window-rain
Rain on the glass.
@cg sea-of-points | The inside of the model
@show Model center
Model: And this is where I live.
@cg off

@scene Tones
@bg lecture
@tone dusk
Dusk.
@tone night
Night.
@tone dawn
Dawn.
@tone noon
Noon.
@tone memory
Memory.
@tone cold
Cold.
@tone none
@card A paper card | pinned: to the scene | ruled: like an index card
@chart bar A chalkboard | this=3 | that=5 ^para
@code js | function f(_lastNSecs) { | return _lastNSecs < 3; | }
You: And that is the whole stage.
@end
